WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:55.260
<b>Adventure
in the Kingdom of Sand</b>

3
00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:00.680
What a nice breeze!

4
00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:14.280
Nami, I'd like to dock
the ship here for a moment.

5
00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:15.780
Huh? What for?

6
00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:18.450
I have an important task for Karoo.

7
00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:19.450
Karoo?

8
00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:27.210
Karoo...

9
00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:31.630
You must go to Alubarna Palace
and deliver this letter to my father.

10
00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:35.510
I have laid out Crocodile
and Baroque Works' scheme.

11
00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:38.600
This is everything
Igaram and I uncovered.

12
00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:43.100
It will also show that I have
returned to Alabasta alive,

13
00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:46.310
and that with me are
powerful friends and allies.

14
00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:49.980
Will you cross
the desert wasteland alone?

15
00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:57.200
Listen. Please conserve
your water while in the desert.

16
00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:00.410
Good luck, Karoo!

17
00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:04.410
Now let my father know
this kingdom can be saved!

18
00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:13.590
And conserve your water!

19
00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:18.930
Karoo, please make it...

20
00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:23.680
I did hear that the Warlord,
Crocodile, was here.

21
00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:27.150
But a pirate stealing a whole country?

22
00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:28.940
Sounds like a bad joke.

23
00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:32.900
A pirate dropping anchor
in one spot and settling down?

24
00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:36.150
Hard to believe he'd actually
try and usurp the throne.

25
00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:37.950
Alright! Let's set sail!

26
00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:40.160
Wait till I'm on board, will you?!

27
00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:43.410
Y'know, this whole takeover
thing could just be a ruse.

28
00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:44.910
A ruse?

29
00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:47.830
A facade with a hidden goal...

30
00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:50.540
We're finally here!

31
00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:52.800
We're really going into the desert!

32
00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:54.510
I wonder how hot it gets...

33
00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:56.420
Over 50 degrees at high noon.

34
00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:57.090
What?!

35
00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:58.590
It does?!

36
00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:01.470
What happened, Nami?!
Where's your dancer outfit?!

37
00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:03.720
What?! You too, Vivi?!

38
00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:05.100
What's with that getup?!

39
00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:09.850
In the desert, any exposed skin
will wind up terribly sunburned!

40
00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:13.570
It's over... My dancer girls...

41
00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:15.190
Put this on, Luffy.

42
00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:16.690
Okay! Thank you!

43
00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:18.070
Let's get ready to disembark.

44
00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:19.160
Sounds good.

45
00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:29.710
Okay! Make landfall!

46
00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:35.170
What's that?

47
00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:42.640
Turtles?

48
00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:44.010
Don't you mean seals?

49
00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:45.260
Kung fu dugongs!

50
00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:49.140
"To come ashore,
you must first best me."

51
00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:51.480
"Otherwise, you cowards
can turn right around."

52
00:04:51.940 --> 00:04:53.060
Is what he says.

53
00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:58.190
Think you can get away with
calling me a "coward"?

54
00:04:58.190 --> 00:04:59.240
Let's do it!

55
00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:00.610
Wait! Usopp!

56
00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:04.700
Kung fu dugongs are known
for their strength!

57
00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:08.540
Well... there's a victory!

58
00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:09.580
That's even worse!

59
00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:14.790
What the...?

60
00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:17.420
This is their code:

61
00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:21.010
when a kung fu dugong loses,
the winner is their new master.

62
00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:22.090
True martial artists.

63
00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:26.850
He keeps gaining pupils!

64
00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:29.180
Listen up, everyone! After me!

65
00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:29.810
Stance!

66
00:05:30.690 --> 00:05:32.310
No! Like this!

67
00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:35.020
Yeah! Now go like this!

68
00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:37.320
That's it! Like this!

69
00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:40.400
Like this! Like this!

70
00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:42.150
Like this!

71
00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:50.870
See ya!

72
00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:53.880
So, Luffy... Do you
understand our new problem?!

73
00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:57.090
They wanted to come with me,
so why won't we let them?

74
00:05:57.090 --> 00:06:00.970
There isn't a single town who'd
let in a group that big, dumbass.

75
00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:02.170
Honestly!

76
00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:05.140
We'd have been screwed
if Chopper hadn't intervened!

77
00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:08.430
Yeah! They kept saying,
"We'll accompany you!"

78
00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:11.480
They'd be right behind us
if we hadn't bribed them with food!

79
00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:15.440
No kidding! You cost us a ton of food!

80
00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:18.400
He's a bona fide troublemaker.

81
00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:18.400
You said it!

82
00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:30.910
What's this?

83
00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:33.040
Is this that town? Yuba?

84
00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:34.790
No.

85
00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:38.960
This is Erumalu. It was once
called the City of Green.

86
00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:40.630
City of Green?

87
00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:43.930
This town stands as a testament

88
00:06:43.930 --> 00:06:47.390
to Baroque Works' devastating
presence in this country.

89
00:06:47.890 --> 00:06:51.100
To what Alabasta 
and its citizens have endured...

90
00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:54.560
Wow!

91
00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:57.480
There's just nothing here!

92
00:06:57.480 --> 00:06:58.770
Yes.

93
00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:01.570
It's nothing but a ghost town now,

94
00:07:01.570 --> 00:07:06.110
yet not long ago,
this city was a verdant paradise.

95
00:07:06.740 --> 00:07:08.240
What, this place?

96
00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:12.660
Rain is already scarce here.

97
00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:16.290
Even so, the city saved every
last drop of rainwater it could,

98
00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:18.500
and as a result it prospered.

99
00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:21.210
But, for three years now,

100
00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:25.340
not a single drop of rain has fallen
in all but one region of this country.

101
00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:26.590
For three years?!

102
00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:27.550
That long?!

103
00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:32.310
But why worry about the rain
when we just crossed an entire river?!

104
00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:35.520
It's true! Why not just pump
the river water into the city?

105
00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:38.440
The answer lies ahead.

106
00:07:43.110 --> 00:07:49.410
Never in the thousands of years of Alabasta's
history has the rain stopped completely.

107
00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:54.330
But one region always tended
toward more rain than the others:

108
00:07:54.830 --> 00:07:56.710
Alubarna, the capital.

109
00:07:57.330 --> 00:07:59.830
The royal palace is in that city.

110
00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:07.130
<b>2 Years Ago</b>

111
00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:23.020
The people called it
"the king's miracle."

112
00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:25.530
That is, until the day of the incident.

113
00:08:25.570 --> 00:08:31.160
<b>The Port Town of Nanohana</b>

114
00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:29.700
Lower the cargo!

115
00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:38.250
It's tipping!

116
00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:39.290
Look out!

117
00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:43.750
Hey! Are you guys okay?!

118
00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:47.970
<b>Half
Fledged</b>

119
00:08:44.340 --> 00:08:46.460
Oh, no! This is bad!

120
00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:50.050
We were supposed to deliver this
to King Cobra in Alubarna!

121
00:08:47.970 --> 00:08:50.050
<b>Half
Fledged</b>

122
00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:53.010
What is this green powder?

123
00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:54.100
What is it?

124
00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:58.350
H-How should we know?!
We're only following your king's orders!

125
00:08:58.350 --> 00:08:58.980
Right?

126
00:08:58.980 --> 00:09:00.350
We're just deliverymen!

127
00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:01.060
– Run!
– Run!

128
00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:07.440
This dust... It can't be!

129
00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:10.030
Dance powder?!

130
00:09:10.530 --> 00:09:12.530
You've heard of it?

131
00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:13.030
Yes.

132
00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:16.200
It's more aptly known
as "rain-summoning powder".

133
00:09:16.580 --> 00:09:17.700
Rain-summoning?

134
00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:19.710
I heard about it secondhand,

135
00:09:19.710 --> 00:09:24.090
but it was supposedly created
by a scientist in a land with no rain.

136
00:09:24.090 --> 00:09:29.300
Combining it with rising smoke
creates a spreading mist in the sky,

137
00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:32.380
which artificially causes rainfall.

138
00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:34.350
And that's dance powder.

139
00:09:34.350 --> 00:09:38.100
The country who created
the powder almost danced for joy,

140
00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:40.810
and that's how it got its name.

141
00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:44.810
However, for every action
there's a reaction.

142
00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:45.770
You see...

143
00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:48.650
the neighboring land
had a sudden drought.

144
00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:49.530
You follow?

145
00:09:49.530 --> 00:09:54.240
Dance powder prematurely
grows clouds by artificial means

146
00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:59.410
before they are given time to become
rain clouds farther downwind,

147
00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:01.460
and forces young clouds to rain.

148
00:10:01.460 --> 00:10:02.080
So–

149
00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:03.040
Oh, I get it!

150
00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:07.840
It steals rain that would've normally
gone to a neighboring country!

151
00:10:08.210 --> 00:10:14.140
As a result, the two countries
went to war, and many lives were lost.

152
00:10:14.140 --> 00:10:17.050
The World Government put
a general ban on dance powder,

153
00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:19.140
prohibiting both production and usage.

154
00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:22.600
Powder that can bring both happiness
and sorrow when used...

155
00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:27.110
When that large shipment of
dance powder arrived at the port town,

156
00:10:27.110 --> 00:10:29.980
Alabasta was in the midst
of a weather phenomenon;

157
00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:33.070
the only place with rainfall
was the king's city.

158
00:10:34.070 --> 00:10:39.330
The rain stopped falling here because
the king is using dance powder!

159
00:10:39.330 --> 00:10:42.790
Alubarna's rain wasn't
a miracle after all!

160
00:10:42.790 --> 00:10:48.000
It's all that king's fault
everyone's parched and starving!

161
00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:51.340
Hold on, Vivi! That means
your dad is the bad guy here!

162
00:10:51.340 --> 00:10:53.720
You idiot! He was obviously framed!

163
00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:56.260
Vivi's father would
never do such a thing!

164
00:10:56.260 --> 00:11:00.220
Never! Never! Never!
Never! Never! Never!

165
00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:05.520
Of course, my father
had nothing to do with it...

166
00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:07.480
but at that time...

167
00:11:08.360 --> 00:11:12.280
a massive amount of dance powder
was discovered inside the palace.

168
00:11:12.780 --> 00:11:15.740
He even had people working
inside the palace?

169
00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:20.530
What kind of road is this, Vivi?

170
00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:25.290
This was an irrigation canal that once
carried water from the Sandora River.

171
00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:29.250
But someone came through
and destroyed it.

172
00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:34.590
With its canal gone, the City of Green
could no longer secure water.

173
00:11:35.380 --> 00:11:40.600
People prayed and held out hope,
but the rain never came.

174
00:11:43.020 --> 00:11:48.060
Ever since the dance powder incident,
distrust in the king grows daily.

175
00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:50.900
All according to Crocodile's plan, huh?

176
00:11:51.360 --> 00:11:54.360
And then the fighting finally began.

177
00:11:55.440 --> 00:12:01.330
The people abandoned their cities,
weary of the constant skirmishes,

178
00:12:01.330 --> 00:12:04.290
and sought out oases
and other sources of water.

179
00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:07.210
And then...

180
00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:11.880
the City of Green withered away.

181
00:12:15.510 --> 00:12:16.630
Someone's collapsed!

182
00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:19.590
There are still people in this city?!

183
00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:31.110
What did my father...?

184
00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:35.480
What did the citizens
of this country ever do?

185
00:12:36.190 --> 00:12:38.320
This country is a harsh desert;

186
00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:40.610
the people struggle
against nature itself!

187
00:12:40.610 --> 00:12:44.160
Yet he has destroyed the lives
they fight so hard to maintain!

188
00:12:44.830 --> 00:12:48.660
What... What gives him
the right to do that?!

189
00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:49.670
What?!

190
00:12:51.250 --> 00:12:54.670
All the while, as one of
the Seven Warlords,

191
00:12:54.670 --> 00:12:56.590
he masquerades as the people's hero!

192
00:12:57.260 --> 00:13:02.430
No one realizes he's
deceiving the entire country!

193
00:13:02.430 --> 00:13:10.100
Crocodile! Crocodile! Crocodile!
Crocodile! Crocodile! Crocodile!

194
00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:11.310
I...

195
00:13:12.020 --> 00:13:14.020
can't let him get away with this!

196
00:13:22.990 --> 00:13:25.910
Really? Grow up already.

197
00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:38.760
Vivi!

198
00:13:39.130 --> 00:13:40.880
Let's get moving!

199
00:13:41.510 --> 00:13:43.050
I'm itching to do this now!

200
00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:47.430
Let's go to Yuba!

201
00:13:48.350 --> 00:13:50.520
The Rebel Army's there, right?

202
00:13:52.020 --> 00:13:55.810
Yes. I will persuade their leader
to end the rebellion.

203
00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:56.650
"Persuade"?

204
00:13:57.020 --> 00:14:00.570
All of Alabasta's calamities
are Crocodile's doing!

205
00:14:00.570 --> 00:14:01.900
Once he knows the truth,

206
00:14:01.900 --> 00:14:04.320
he will stop this pointless bloodshed!

207
00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:05.570
Got it.

208
00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:24.550
So hot... Water...

209
00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:32.480
Burning up... Sweat
won't even come out...

210
00:14:32.850 --> 00:14:36.860
Quit moaning so much, Luffy.
You'll only tire yourself out.

211
00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:39.820
Guess he's not listening.

212
00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:46.410
I can't go on. I can't take the heat.

213
00:14:46.410 --> 00:14:49.410
Cold weather, though? That's fine.

214
00:14:49.410 --> 00:14:53.790
It's all that fur. Just take off
your animal costume.

215
00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:56.920
You want me to do what now?

216
00:14:56.920 --> 00:14:59.550
You making fun of this reindeer?!

217
00:14:59.550 --> 00:15:01.510
Monster!

218
00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:05.130
Chopper! Turn big again
and the free ride is over!

219
00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:07.890
Who're you calling
a monster, monster-nose?!

220
00:15:07.890 --> 00:15:10.390
D-Don't be fooled!
I-I'll have you know this nose–

221
00:15:10.390 --> 00:15:12.600
Just change back already!

222
00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:17.060
You don't seem to be
having a hard time, Vivi.

223
00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:20.770
I was born and raised here,
so it doesn't bother me much.

224
00:15:20.770 --> 00:15:24.150
But... what's with all these hills?!

225
00:15:24.150 --> 00:15:27.740
I figured a desert would be more flat.

226
00:15:28.990 --> 00:15:31.790
This is a very old desert,

227
00:15:31.790 --> 00:15:35.040
so some sand dunes here
are over 300 meters high.

228
00:15:35.040 --> 00:15:37.170
Th-Three hundred meters?

229
00:15:37.170 --> 00:15:39.460
So that's why it's like...
climbing mountains...!

230
00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:43.460
It's too much... It's so hot...

231
00:15:43.840 --> 00:15:47.180
Just one drink, Luffy.
Just one mouthful.

232
00:15:49.430 --> 00:15:50.180
Too much!

233
00:15:50.180 --> 00:15:53.060
I'd like some too!
You just had thirteen mouthfuls!

234
00:15:53.060 --> 00:15:56.140
Not yet! You just had some! I'm next!

235
00:15:56.140 --> 00:15:59.730
Stop fighting! That's
how you waste energy!

236
00:16:00.190 --> 00:16:01.650
But she started it!

237
00:16:01.650 --> 00:16:02.980
It's your fault!

238
00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:04.740
Yeah! This is because of you!

239
00:16:04.740 --> 00:16:05.650
What?!

240
00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:10.280
Hey! Sanji! Let's have lunch!
A pirate lunch!

241
00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:13.700
Not yet. Not until Vivi says so.

242
00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:17.580
Come on, Vivi!
Let's eat! I'm outta strength!

243
00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:22.500
But we're only one tenth
of the way to Yuba, Luffy.

244
00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:25.670
How can you be so smart
if you haven't heard the old saying:

245
00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:27.760
"If you're hungry, eat!"?

246
00:16:27.760 --> 00:16:30.220
You liar! Quit making stuff up!

247
00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:31.850
All right.

248
00:16:31.850 --> 00:16:35.100
How about we stop
at the next rocky area?

249
00:16:35.100 --> 00:16:36.560
Cool! Looking for rocks!

250
00:16:36.560 --> 00:16:39.350
Everyone! We're gonna hurry
to the next rocky area!

251
00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:42.560
Whoever wins Rock Paper Scissors
carries everyone's stuff!

252
00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:43.900
Quit deciding things!

253
00:16:46.780 --> 00:16:50.740
H-Heavy... So heavy... And hot...

254
00:16:50.740 --> 00:16:52.990
I won Rock Paper Scissors,
so why me?

255
00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:56.750
It's because you won.
Now shut up and haul.

256
00:16:56.750 --> 00:16:58.500
Don't drop it, now!

257
00:17:05.420 --> 00:17:07.880
Hey! Rocky outcropping,
dead ahead!

258
00:17:08.260 --> 00:17:09.260
Really?!

259
00:17:09.630 --> 00:17:12.760
Break time! Food!

260
00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:14.720
Whoa! He's fast!

261
00:17:18.640 --> 00:17:22.650
Finally! Shade! Feels so good!

262
00:17:41.420 --> 00:17:43.960
Bad news!

263
00:17:43.960 --> 00:17:46.040
And just like that, he's coming back?

264
00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:49.880
There's this group of birds
in real bad shape! Chopper!

265
00:17:50.630 --> 00:17:51.880
Right!

266
00:17:52.680 --> 00:17:55.010
Alright! Let's go, Chopper!

267
00:17:55.010 --> 00:17:55.800
Yeah!

268
00:17:56.350 --> 00:17:58.180
We gotta help these birds!

269
00:17:58.180 --> 00:17:59.060
Birds?!

270
00:17:59.060 --> 00:18:01.770
Wait, Luffy! These birds
sound like... Oh, no!

271
00:18:03.150 --> 00:18:04.020
Huh?

272
00:18:06.980 --> 00:18:08.650
They robbed us blind!

273
00:18:08.650 --> 00:18:10.490
We've been had...

274
00:18:11.280 --> 00:18:15.570
It's true, though! The birds here were
really about to kick the bucket!

275
00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:17.450
I'm sorry.

276
00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:19.490
I should have informed you sooner.

277
00:18:20.500 --> 00:18:24.960
Rogue herons, or desert bandits,
trick travelers and steal their supplies.

278
00:18:24.960 --> 00:18:27.420
What?!

279
00:18:28.420 --> 00:18:32.220
The birds play dead?
What a buncha liars!

280
00:18:32.220 --> 00:18:34.220
Yes, that's their nature.

281
00:18:34.220 --> 00:18:35.890
Then they tricked me!

282
00:18:35.890 --> 00:18:38.680
Luffy! Is that all you can
say for yourself?!

283
00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:41.180
We packed three days'
worth of provisions,

284
00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:43.350
and you let those birds
take everything!

285
00:18:43.350 --> 00:18:48.480
We're smack dab in the middle of a desert
without even a change of clothes!

286
00:18:48.480 --> 00:18:51.610
How do we cross a desert
when there's no food or water?!

287
00:18:51.610 --> 00:18:54.860
It's not my fault. They tricked me.

288
00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:57.280
How are you dumber than a bird?!

289
00:18:57.280 --> 00:18:58.240
Dumber than what?!

290
00:18:58.740 --> 00:19:00.290
Stop it, you two!

291
00:19:01.870 --> 00:19:03.160
It's no use.

292
00:19:03.660 --> 00:19:07.540
At times like this,
it's best to let them have it out.

293
00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:09.920
Fair point.

294
00:19:11.090 --> 00:19:14.550
Let's take a short break.
This heat is melting their brains.

295
00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:17.720
Food-wise, we'll manage.

296
00:19:18.220 --> 00:19:22.020
Being hungry hasn't killed us yet.
No use thinking about it.

297
00:19:22.020 --> 00:19:25.480
Yeah. Those thoughts
just get me thirstier.

298
00:19:38.870 --> 00:19:42.990
Give us our stuff back!

299
00:19:42.990 --> 00:19:45.370
Luffy! Don't chase them!

300
00:19:45.370 --> 00:19:46.710
That birdbrain.

301
00:19:46.710 --> 00:19:49.580
Hey! You'll lose your way back!

302
00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:52.300
Just come back, Luffy!

303
00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:58.260
Stop! You can't get away from me!

304
00:20:03.850 --> 00:20:05.560
Get back here!

305
00:20:09.900 --> 00:20:12.150
What's taking Luffy so long?!

306
00:20:12.770 --> 00:20:15.860
Yeah. Do you think he got lost?

307
00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:19.660
Luffy is dreadfully unaware
of the all the desert dangers.

308
00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:23.200
What's that?!

309
00:20:29.670 --> 00:20:31.540
What's this rumbling?!

310
00:20:38.840 --> 00:20:41.220
Another sandstorm?!

311
00:20:41.930 --> 00:20:44.060
No, wait! That's...

312
00:20:47.310 --> 00:20:48.140
Luffy!

313
00:20:48.520 --> 00:20:50.650
No... it's not possible!

314
00:20:53.480 --> 00:20:56.030
Why is he on a camel?!

315
00:20:58.280 --> 00:21:01.160
Not important! What's chasing him?!

316
00:21:01.160 --> 00:21:02.280
Hard to tell!

317
00:21:02.280 --> 00:21:05.490
It looks like something's
surging through the sand!

318
00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:12.080
It's huge!

319
00:21:11.210 --> 00:21:12.080
What the...?!

320
00:21:12.420 --> 00:21:13.790
A Sandora dragon!

321
00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:15.300
A-A-A wh-what now?!

322
00:21:15.300 --> 00:21:20.800
The largest of the desert's reptiles,
they wait under the sand for their prey!

323
00:21:20.800 --> 00:21:25.350
They have sharp claws and teeth,
but they rarely need to use them!

324
00:21:25.350 --> 00:21:30.230
They are so big, they tend
to just swallow their prey whole!

325
00:21:30.730 --> 00:21:34.190
He really does have a gift
for attracting trouble.

326
00:21:34.190 --> 00:21:36.820
We can settle the camel thing later.

327
00:21:36.820 --> 00:21:40.740
What star was he born under
to become such a magnet for trouble?!

328
00:21:40.740 --> 00:21:42.990
Hey! Camel! Stop!

329
00:21:44.740 --> 00:21:46.490
Luffy! In over your head?!

330
00:21:46.490 --> 00:21:47.870
We'll lend a hand!

331
00:21:47.870 --> 00:21:49.620
Yeah! I brought some meat!

332
00:21:49.620 --> 00:21:51.000
Here goes, lizard!

333
00:21:51.000 --> 00:21:51.870
Gum-Gum...

334
00:21:51.870 --> 00:21:52.540
Dragon...

335
00:21:52.540 --> 00:21:53.460
Épaule...

336
00:21:53.460 --> 00:21:53.960
Whip!

337
00:21:53.960 --> 00:21:54.500
Twister!

338
00:21:54.500 --> 00:21:55.090
Shoot!

339
00:22:03.800 --> 00:22:05.550
Wh-Why take things so far?

340
00:22:05.550 --> 00:22:09.020
When they're fighting,
you almost pity the monsters.

341
00:22:16.860 --> 00:22:20.320
Check it out! These rocks
are natural frying pans!

342
00:22:21.360 --> 00:22:24.530
So, what's with the camel?

343
00:22:26.320 --> 00:22:27.080
Dunno.

344
00:22:27.080 --> 00:22:30.660
I saw a mystery plant trying to eat it
while I was chasing the birds.

345
00:22:30.660 --> 00:22:32.830
It doesn't seem to be a wild camel.

346
00:22:32.830 --> 00:22:35.750
No. It even has a saddle.

347
00:22:36.880 --> 00:22:40.840
Great, so we can ride it?!
What a lucky break!

348
00:22:40.840 --> 00:22:44.300
Yeah, that'll be a real help!
Looks like there's room for two!

349
00:22:44.680 --> 00:22:47.180
Camels do go hand-in-hand
with deserts!

350
00:22:47.180 --> 00:22:49.470
Then don't mind if I–

351
00:22:50.680 --> 00:22:51.680
What's your deal?!

352
00:22:52.180 --> 00:22:55.940
"I am a freedom-loving, hard-boiled,
compassionate camel!"

353
00:22:55.940 --> 00:22:58.940
"Thanks for helping me out back there."

354
00:22:58.940 --> 00:23:02.530
"I can give anyone a lift
as long as they're not a man."

355
00:23:06.110 --> 00:23:07.660
"I'm manly!"

356
00:23:08.450 --> 00:23:10.990
– Quit being stupid!
– Why, you...!

357
00:23:12.330 --> 00:23:16.330
You poor thing! My crewmates
weren't bred for manners.

358
00:23:16.330 --> 00:23:18.920
I think you're a good boy!
What should we call you?

359
00:23:18.920 --> 00:23:19.920
Idiot!

360
00:23:19.920 --> 00:23:20.590
Moron!

361
00:23:20.590 --> 00:23:21.380
Dumbass!

362
00:23:21.380 --> 00:23:23.050
Eyelashes it is, then!

363
00:23:23.050 --> 00:23:25.430
Um, that's the weirdest
one of the bunch.

364
00:23:26.010 --> 00:23:27.840
Okay! Get on, Vivi!

365
00:23:27.840 --> 00:23:30.810
No, I can still walk!

366
00:23:30.810 --> 00:23:31.720
Just get on.

367
00:23:31.720 --> 00:23:32.680
He's a pervy camel!

368
00:23:32.680 --> 00:23:33.480
Pervy camel!

369
00:23:33.480 --> 00:23:37.190
– Pervy camel! Pervy camel!
– Pervy camel! Pervy camel!

370
00:23:37.770 --> 00:23:40.440
We'll get there
a little faster now, right?

371
00:23:40.440 --> 00:23:44.490
The sooner we get to Yuba,
the sooner you talk to the Rebel Army!

372
00:23:45.030 --> 00:23:46.240
Giddyup, Eyelashes!

373
00:23:47.570 --> 00:23:48.910
Wait up!

374
00:23:49.370 --> 00:23:53.500
Hurry, guys! If we get separated,
you'll never leave the desert alive!

375
00:23:53.500 --> 00:23:54.500
You're the worst!

376
00:23:54.500 --> 00:23:56.500
But I still love you, Nami!

377
00:23:56.500 --> 00:23:57.750
After them! Hurry!

378
00:23:57.750 --> 00:23:58.710
Get on, Chopper!

379
00:23:58.710 --> 00:23:59.500
Yeah!

380
00:23:59.500 --> 00:24:01.540
– Wait for us!
– Wait for us!
